  "summary": "I enjoy the process of creating new things, and then improving on them.  In my career as a tester, this has often involved helping developers find bugs to make our product better – but has also shown up in automation that I've done, and suggestions that I've made, to make our automation more user-friendly.  I like to think that I have a good sense of humor – and like to try to make my coworkers laugh when I run into them in the hallways, or we're out at lunch.   \n\nI love the current indie scene in videogames.  Many small developers are taking risks to make games that are unique and fascinating while, due to the cost of making a triple-A title, most of the biggest companies release slight modifications on a formula that they know will be sell well, and recoup their investment.  Firewatch, Life is Strange, Gone Home, The Vanishing of Ethan Carter, Thomas Was Alone, Actual Sunlight, Braid, Her Story, Three Fourths Home.  \n\nI've always been a fan of old school RPGs like Final Fantasy VI, IV, and X.  But a few years ago, I played 999 - 9 Hours, 9 Persons, 9 Doors - and it was a revelation to me.  Almost entirely text (with the occasional puzzle), I found that the music helped heighten the tension and mood.  I tried to track down everything that I could that was even remotely similar.  Pheonix Wright, Trace Memory, Ghost Trick: Phantom Detective, Corpse Party.  I've since played the rest of the Zero Escape series as they've come out, as well as the DanganRonpa series.\n\nI look at the world in a slightly different way than most people, and have many unique ideas of my own.  I would love to find a place where I can bring my creativity to the table, and collaborate with a great team to help create something special.",
